Rule 5 which deals with functions of the laboratory reads as follows:-
"5. Functions of Laboratory.--The functions of the Laboratory shall be as follows-- (a) to analyse such samples of insecticides sent to it under the Act by any officer or authority authorised by the Central or State Governments - 25 - NC: 2024:KHC:51578 AND 10 OTHERS and submission of certificates of analysis to the authority concerned;
(b) to analyse samples of materials for insecticide residues under the provisions of the Act;
(c) to carry out such investigations as may be necessary for the purpose of ensuring the conditions of Registration of insecticides;
(d) to determine the efficacy and toxicity of insecticides;
(e) to carry out such other functions as may be entrusted to it by the Central Government or by a State Government with the permission of the Central Government and after consultation with the Board."
Rule 5 deals with various functions from analysis to reporting of a sample that is drawn and sent to it either by the State Government or the Central Government.
